on-actor.ts, loaded lazily) uses the same functions as createHistoryEntry, so a guard judges exactly the identity history records. runActiveBeforeMutationHooks takes the author instead of a prebuilt context. previewItemMutations and structured CLI previews evaluate the caller's guards against the staged plan with dry_run true and the commit's actor; the unresolved constraint is renamed extension_write_hooks. pm delete --dry-run passes dry_run. Package imports (commitImportedItem, operation import) and pm copy now run guards, with body in changed_fields. Import guards judge the canonical document that is persisted, and only a held lock is a skippable conflict. The test harness resolves an omitted actor from the author. Spec: tests/unit/sdk/extension/mutation-guard-actor.spec.ts covers a claimant-only close through the SDK client, CLI and MCP, preview/commit actor parity, delete dry run, copy and import."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"beforeMutation guards receive a frozen actor block resolved from the mutation's own author, plus dry_run; previews judge guards as dry runs; imports and copies are guarded"}],"before_hash":"f287973c6cc99d860ea31ff90dcdf623fa113086dfc880459893653adb8e7037","after_hash":"692b3a2fd22840c7a410c122481b3d07076a12ddb4fbd50cd7207ca24fd0d22a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T09:04:24.317Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4449a80344da60e7090663a89e4f55b1341cdedfca13213268d444a844cfea0d"}
